recursive-include vectors *.json
# The vectors are the normative artifact, and the fixture grammar is what makes
# them readable — an sdist that ships the JSON without it hands a port author
# data with no semantics.
recursive-include vectors *.md
# And the gate that spec tells them to run. It is stdlib-only for exactly this
# reason (its vocabularies are hand-copied so it needs no atlas import), and it
# resolves the corpus relative to its own parent directory, so it works from an
# unpacked sdist as it does in the repo. The breaking-change gate deliberately
# stays behind: it diffs against git history, which an sdist does not carry.
include scripts/validate_vectors.py
